          <Pad Id="e6ZNsoG4nAVjOBJ2KGkgAr" Bounds="85,85,520,94" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Toggle [Qt]&#xD;&#xA;- Channel: binds the state, the user writes back (IOBox true = start value)&#xD;&#xA;- Value: current state&#xD;&#xA;- Bang: true for one frame when the user flipped it&#xD;&#xA;- Look: Checkbox (default) or Switch">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="J9IBOYBZK3ydysbeadZGeS" Bounds="85,910,830,78" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- A plain value or an IOBox on Channel is the start value and sets the state from the patch. The state survives a Look change.&#xD;&#xA;- A Counter counts the flips (Bang).&#xD;&#xA;- Labels are not part of the toggle: wrap it in a Labeled element (here a Column stacks the Labeled toggles).">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
